---
title: MP3 upload and result sequence
query: >-
  Show the implemented Analyze MP3 request and response sequence through the browser, NGINX, native Node API and
  pure parser. Include local file validation, pending controls, the actual-byte 20 MiB bound, typed parser failures,
  proxy failures, JSON validation and restored controls after every outcome. Count complete physical MPEG-1 Layer III
  frames including metadata-bearing frames. Keep errors readable and show that aborted uploads cannot succeed.
  Use only behavior supported by the referenced files; this is not a cloud deployment diagram.
  Group NGINX inside the frontend Docker container and API plus parser inside the API Docker container. The API and
  parser share one Node process; browser JavaScript runs outside Docker. Never draw the parser as a third container.
references:
  - "File: /frontend/app.js"
  - "File: /frontend/nginx.conf.template"
  - "File: /server/src/http.ts"
  - "File: /server/src/mp3.ts"
  - "File: /frontend/Dockerfile"
  - "File: /server/Dockerfile"
  - "File: /compose.yaml"
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant Browser as Browser runs app.js
    box rgb(224,242,254) Frontend Docker container
        participant Frontend as NGINX :8080
    end
    box rgb(220,252,231) API Docker container - one Node process
        participant API as Node HTTP :3000
        participant Parser as In-process parser
    end
    User->>Browser: Select file and Analyze MP3
    alt Missing file or file exceeds 20 MiB
        Browser-->>User: Readable local error
    else File passes local validation
        Browser->>Browser: Set pending, disable duplicate submit, start deadline
        Browser->>Frontend: Raw POST /file-upload via published loopback port
        alt Ingress rejection or unavailable/timed-out upstream
            Frontend-->>Browser: Error status and JSON
        else Request forwarded over HTTP/1.1 without buffering or retry
            Frontend->>API: Forward raw bytes to api:3000 on Compose network
            API->>API: Validate headers, admission and actual received bytes
            alt Invalid request, over limit, busy or timed out
                API-->>Frontend: Contracted error status and JSON
            else Complete nonempty body within 20 MiB
                API->>Parser: Count complete physical MPEG-1 Layer III frames
                alt Valid supported file
                    Parser-->>API: Positive count including metadata-bearing frames
                    API-->>Frontend: 200 JSON with frameCount
                else Invalid or unsupported structure
                    Parser-->>API: Typed failure
                    API-->>Frontend: 400 or 415 JSON
                end
            end
            Frontend-->>Browser: Preserve API status and JSON
        end
        Browser->>Browser: Validate JSON and exact success shape
        Browser-->>User: Count or readable error#59; allow retry
        Browser->>Browser: Always clear deadline and restore controls
    end
    Note over Browser,API: Abort or network failure is not partial success
    Note over API,Parser: Release bounded upload memory#59; no MediaInfo, retained upload or background job
